WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.960
Okay, so if I'm just being honest here,

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:06.720
I can't help but notice that there are a

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.559
lot of videos here on YouTube where

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.880
creators are talking about all these

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:12.480
great AI business ideas that they have.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.120
Yet, very few of them are actually

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.840
showing how they themselves are using AI

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.520
tools to make money. But I have I have

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.840
case studies on this channel showing how

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.960
I built my one person AI business to

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.439
over $1,000 a day. So, I know how to

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.519
actually do it. I know how to use AI to

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:31.679
automate creating products or services,

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:33.920
getting free sales and traffic, and

00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:36.719
crucially identifying low competition

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.800
niches to target. And that word automate

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:40.399
is key. Because, as I'm sure a lot of

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.480
you can relate, when I first started

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:44.879
this side hustle, I was already working

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.480
over 40 hours a week. So, I've had to

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:48.640
figure out how to automate as much as

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.960
possible to be able to stack it as an

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.600
additional income source on top of what

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.440
I already do and earn. So, let me show

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.239
you how I do this so that you can copy

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.079
my AI tool workflows. But first, I know

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:02.000
from my analytics most people to my

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:04.640
channel are new and haven't seen my

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.560
previous case studies on my AI business.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.640
So, I'll quickly explain what it is and

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.720
how it makes money so that all of us are

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.479
on the same page. Basically, it's pretty

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.080
simple. I just create fun print on

00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:16.400
demand products like clothes that I

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.720
design using AI tools, which I then sell

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.640
on Etsy for a profit. My idea to start

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.640
the store came one day when I was on

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.799
Etsy looking for funny, clever dog

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.720
clothing. And while I did find some good

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.640
shirts that I was willing to buy, they

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.360
were about dogs in general, there were

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.840
no good, clever shirts about specific

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.720
dog breeds such as huskys or corgis that

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.720
I liked and was willing to actually buy.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.040
And when I noticed this, I realized I

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.880
had discovered this a gap in the market.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.880
This is when there is demand for a

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.280
product or a service or even say a

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.840
YouTube channel, but it either hasn't

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.240
yet been made or there is not enough of

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.240
it to meet the demand. And so, of

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.280
course, I decided to fill that gap

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.520
myself. I used AI LLM chat bots like

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:01.680
Gemini, ChatGpt, and Claude to

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.920
brainstorm fun clothing slogans. And I

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.320
used AI tools to take those ideas and

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.399
then turn them into actual designs. And

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.720
then I came to print on demand apps like

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:12.400
Printify, which have a huge catalog of

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:14.800
blank products that you can customize

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.640
and sell, such as t-shirts, by uploading

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.239
the designs you create onto them, and

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.400
then listing them in your store for a

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:22.800
markup price. So, I of course listed

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.560
them in my new Etsy store. And well,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.560
since Etsy already gets hundreds of

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.800
millions of visits each month, I got my

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.040
traffic to my listings by using AI chat

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.360
bots like Claude to optimize my products

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.360
for Etsy's algorithm to be able to piggy

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.160
back off of this traffic already coming

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.000
into the website anyway. And it worked.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.400
Within two weeks, I had my first two

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.400
sales and well, it has snowballed from

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.720
there. And so now, every week, Etsy

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.879
quietly sends me a check while my store

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.879
runs on its own semi-passively as an

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:52.480
extra income source for me. Because the

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:54.160
way that it works is that each time

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.239
somebody buys one of my products, the

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.160
Printify print shop will print my design

00:02:56.239 --> 00:03:00.239
onto the product, package it up, and

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.400
ship it out to my customer while I get

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:04.400
to keep the difference as profit. So,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.159
yeah, it's mostly hands-off now that

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.920
it's set up and running. And if you'd

00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:09.920
like to learn even more about how it

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.239
works, you can download a copy of my

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.840
free ebook, My One Person AI Business

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:15.440
Unlocked. You can find a link to

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.840
download my free ebook in the video

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.680
description below. But yes, now that

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.280
everyone is on the same page, let's

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.440
discuss the three steps that I followed

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.519
to first choose a business idea that I

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.840
thought would work well as a second side

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:30.400
income source, automate it, and then

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.040
importantly, how I got free traffic to

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.400
it. So, let's start with step one. You

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.159
of course need to choose whatever

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.319
business or side hustle that you're

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:40.560
going to start. And for me, I chose to

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:42.239
start one that I already had an unfair

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.519
advantage in. Because here's the thing,

00:03:42.239 --> 00:03:45.760
right? If you're trying to stack a

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:48.000
second income on top of an already busy

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:50.239
work schedule like I was, you kind of

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.560
need to make it as easy for yourself as

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:54.319
possible, you know. And for me, I knew I

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.560
had an unfair advantage when it came to

00:03:54.319 --> 00:03:59.360
starting a store about dog themed merch.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.120
And that's because I myself love dogs. I

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.439
was already buying dog themed products

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.680
for myself anyway. And so, because I

00:04:03.439 --> 00:04:07.599
myself am a customer in this niche, it

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.360
made it easier for me to have fast

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:11.760
success in it. Because here is a

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.000
question for you. Yes, it is super easy

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.639
for anyone to come up with a t-shirt

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.639
design and go to AI and get it to make

00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:20.639
50 different images to pick from to

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:22.880
sell. But here's a question. You can't

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:25.360
upload all of these to Etsy. So all of

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.680
these 50 images, they are different.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.000
Which one is the best? Which one would

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.759
customers like the most? And actually,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.320
we can make this question even more

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:36.960
tricky because AI image generators let

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.040
you make modifications to the images

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.880
that it makes. So, here's the new

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.280
tougher question for you. Which of these

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:45.360
designs in its current form maybe is not

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.360
the best, but if we were to make a

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.840
change to it, we could turn it into the

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.320
best design. It's tricky, isn't it? And

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:54.479
so, that is where my unfair advantage

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.560
comes in because, well, since I myself

00:04:54.479 --> 00:04:59.120
am a customer in this niche, I get to

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.600
use myself as a yard stick. I get to ask

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.840
myself, hm, which of these images do I

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:06.320
like the best and which one would I buy

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.240
if I saw it printed onto a product? And

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.320
so what I actually ended up doing was I

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.320
took two of the pictures and I combined

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:15.680
the best elements of each together into

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:17.440
a single design that was super cool. But

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:20.160
this would have been so much harder and

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:22.400
honestly much slower if I myself didn't

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.560
already understand what customers in the

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.240
niche wanted. And so even though I poked

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:28.479
fun earlier at how there are so many

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:29.759
business idea videos on YouTube, I don't

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:31.199
actually think that these are bad at

00:05:29.759 --> 00:05:33.199
all. In fact, I think that they can

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:35.520
actually be super helpful, which is why

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:37.280
I myself make them. Because while

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.199
watching these, you can learn about lots

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:41.520
of different business ideas and find one

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:43.680
that works well for you with your unique

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.919
advantages. For example, I recently

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:47.440
showcased in a video a very cool side

00:05:45.919 --> 00:05:49.120
hustle people are doing where they

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.440
create these AI fashion models on

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.199
Instagram. They use AI video generators

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:55.120
to create models that are wearing and

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:57.360
showcasing clothing that is up for sale

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:59.280
on Amazon. And then they make money by

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.000
posting affiliate links to where people

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:04.000
can go and buy them on Amazon. It's a

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.560
great strategy. Although, if I'm being

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.639
honest, long-term, this would not be a

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:10.400
good side hustle for me to start because

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:12.479
I myself don't really keep up with

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.880
fashion trends. You know, long-term, I

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:16.800
would find it difficult and boring to

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.960
pick trendy clothes for my models to

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.639
wear. But for someone that did keep up

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.520
with fashion, well, this could be a

00:06:20.639 --> 00:06:26.080
really fun and even easy side hustle for

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:28.000
them to start. And actually, this leads

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.840
me onto my bonus tip. And that is I

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:32.080
truly believe that starting a successful

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:34.160
business is even easier if you can

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.720
identify a problem that people are

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:38.160
having and solve it. Because here's the

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.240
thing, right? When I first launched the

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:42.400
store, I got my first two sales pretty

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.479
fast. And so, the reason why I think I

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.800
got my first sales so quickly was

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:48.720
because I did this. I found a gap in the

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.800
market. People wanted more options for

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.360
clothing related to specific dog breeds.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.039
And so, I made it for them. I filled the

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:56.720
gap in the market, which is great

00:06:55.039 --> 00:06:58.960
because you think about it, right? When

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.440
I first launched my store, I had no

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.280
reviews and I had no social proof. So,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.199
if I had done what I see most other

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.919
beginners honestly do, which is just

00:07:05.199 --> 00:07:09.919
copy t-shirts in already successful Etsy

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:12.160
stores, then why would someone come and

00:07:09.919 --> 00:07:14.639
buy from me when they can just go and

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:17.120
buy from the established Etsy store that

00:07:14.639 --> 00:07:18.880
has reviews and has social proof? So, I

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.120
had to give them a reason to buy from me

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:22.880
and take a chance on me. I had to create

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.800
something new that they wanted. And

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.479
filling a gap is actually a pretty

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:28.080
straightforward way to do that. And

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:29.759
there are lots of ways to fill gaps.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.520
Maybe people want more videos in a

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:33.440
particular niche or genre here on

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:35.599
YouTube. You can make those videos for

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.759
them. Or maybe local businesses in your

00:07:35.599 --> 00:07:39.919
city want or need people to offer a

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:41.759
particular marketing service. Well, you

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:44.000
can go out there and you can offer that

00:07:41.759 --> 00:07:45.280
service to them. However, the next

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.599
question you're probably thinking is

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:49.520
this. Okay, Sarah, but how can I find a

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:51.440
gap in the market to fill? And that's a

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:53.599
good question because it's true. I did

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:56.000
get a bit lucky when I stumbled on mine.

00:07:53.599 --> 00:07:58.080
So rather than wait until you get lucky

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.080
like me, you can always just go and make

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.840
your own luck instead. Take whatever

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.160
niche or business idea you picked in

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:05.840
step one and ask an AI chatbot to do

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:07.840
deep research online and find

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:09.520
discussions from people within the niche

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.120
talking about what problems they are

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.960
having. So let's say that you had

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.800
decided that you would be great at

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.639
making digital products for teachers

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.879
back in step one. Well, you could get an

00:08:16.639 --> 00:08:20.639
AI to research problems that teachers

00:08:18.879 --> 00:08:21.919
are currently struggling with, and then

00:08:20.639 --> 00:08:24.160
you could come up with some sort of

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:26.639
product, video, or app designed to solve

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:28.800
it. So, then onto the next step. But

00:08:26.639 --> 00:08:30.400
first, can I just ask a quick favor? If

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.000
you are enjoying this video, please

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.760
consider giving it a like. Because

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.240
lately, there has been a bit of what

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.399
I've begun to call an AI witch hunt.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:40.800
People are clicking on AI tutorials like

00:08:38.399 --> 00:08:42.880
mine just to leave comments like this,

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.640
which is why it does mean a lot to me

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:46.640
when people leave supportive comments on

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.720
the channel or do click like. So,

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.880
genuinely, thank you so much to everyone

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.560
who supports the channel. But yes, once

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.120
you have your business idea, we can move

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.519
on to step two and create an AI workflow

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.279
for your new business or side hustle.

00:08:57.519 --> 00:09:01.760
And of course, whatever your workflow

00:08:59.279 --> 00:09:03.760
ends up being will depend entirely upon

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:06.160
what business idea or side hustle you

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:08.399
have decided to start. But here's my

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.959
workflow just as an example. First, I

00:09:08.399 --> 00:09:12.720
use Chat GPT Claude or Gemini to help me

00:09:10.959 --> 00:09:14.800
brainstorm niche clothing ideas and

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.640
slogans. Then next, I use Google's

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:18.800
advanced image generator, Nano Banana

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:20.480
Pro, to make the images for me, which I

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:22.560
often access through Higsfield. This is

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.560
an all-in-one media generator that has

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:26.399
all of the most popular image and video

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:28.399
models included in it, which I find

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:30.399
pretty useful since it lets me pay for

00:09:28.399 --> 00:09:33.120
just one subscription to be able to

00:09:30.399 --> 00:09:35.279
access all of these. Then next up, once

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:37.600
I have my design created, I'll upload it

00:09:35.279 --> 00:09:38.880
into the AI powered graphics app, Canva,

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:41.279
and I'll use some of the features

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.200
included in the pro version of Canva to

00:09:41.279 --> 00:09:45.440
make a few tweaks to the design to turn

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.519
it into a print ready file. So, first

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:49.680
I'll use it AI background remover to get

00:09:47.519 --> 00:09:51.600
rid of the white background because if I

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:53.839
don't do that, the image will print like

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:56.000
this onto a t-shirt instead of like

00:09:53.839 --> 00:09:58.160
this. Then next, I'll use Canvas AI

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.320
upscaler to upscale it into high

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.720
resolution so that it will print crisp

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.480
and clear onto products I sell. And then

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:07.040
I just download and export it in two

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:09.360
times resolution as a PNG file with the

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.519
background set to be transparent. And

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:13.440
that's it. I now have my design ready to

00:10:11.519 --> 00:10:15.600
be uploaded and sold onto print on

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:17.920
demand products like clothing, mugs,

