the algorithm works. And so let me show

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:37.039
you the algorithm is basically split

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:39.039
into three distinct phases. Each product

00:20:37.039 --> 00:20:41.200
posted on the platform will go through

00:20:39.039 --> 00:20:43.200
this three-phase algorithm. The first

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:45.360
phase is the test impression phase. And

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:47.360
this is arguably the most important of

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:49.360
all of them to get right. Because you

00:20:47.360 --> 00:20:50.880
see, let's say, for example, that I

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:53.200
decided that you know what, I'm just

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:55.840
going to post this design as a print on

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:57.840
demand mug and list it for sale on Etsy.

00:20:55.840 --> 00:21:00.240
Well, when I do, Etsy's AI will look

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:02.480
over the mug that I uploaded and analyze

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:04.240
its pictures, title, description, tags,

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:06.159
and it will try to guess who out of

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:08.480
their tens of millions of active

00:21:06.159 --> 00:21:10.559
customers might want to buy it. Then, it

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:12.320
will pick a small test group and boost

00:21:10.559 --> 00:21:14.159
my product by putting it in front of

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:16.240
them on places like their homepage,

00:21:14.159 --> 00:21:18.000
their app, or their search results. I

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:20.080
call these test impressions because

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.320
that's what this boost is. It's a test

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:24.080
to see if when showing your product,

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:26.400
will the small group of users that it's

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:28.880
selected actually engage with it, such

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:31.039
as clicking on it or even better, buying

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:33.679
it. Then next up, the product will move

00:21:31.039 --> 00:21:35.679
into phase two, the results. And really,

00:21:33.679 --> 00:21:37.360
this is exactly what it sounds like. The

00:21:35.679 --> 00:21:39.760
algorithm will now analyze whether the

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:41.520
test was successful. If it wasn't and it

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:43.120
didn't get enough engagement, the test

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:45.120
will fizzle and Etsy will stop

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:47.280
artificially boosting the product. But

00:21:45.120 --> 00:21:49.280
on the flip side, if it does pass this

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:51.520
test, then the mug will move on to phase

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:53.760
three, snowball expansion, which is

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:55.360
again exactly what it sounds like. At

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:57.440
this point, the Etsy algorithm will now

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.240
switch to analyzing the people that did

00:21:57.440 --> 00:22:02.320
engage and try to identify other similar

00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:03.919
customers in its database to them. And

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:05.600
it will then expand the test group to

00:22:03.919 --> 00:22:07.200
include those customers. And if it

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:09.440
passes that test, then it will expand

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:12.080
out to even more customers, creating a

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:14.080
snowball viral effect. It's pretty cool.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:15.919
And also, I think it's pretty fair

00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:17.840
because Etsy will generally test all

00:22:15.919 --> 00:22:20.080
products, including products in both new

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:22.400
stores and established stores with this

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:24.559
algorithm, meaning everyone has a chance

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:26.559
for their products to go viral and sell

00:22:24.559 --> 00:22:28.640
if they're actually good, even if you

00:22:26.559 --> 00:22:30.640
don't have any social media followers or

00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:32.960
reviews. And there is a technical name

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:34.960
for a fair algorithm like this. It's

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:37.039
called a multi-armed bandit algorithm,

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.039
if you're curious. But yes, pretty much

00:22:37.039 --> 00:22:41.280
all of the major platforms these days

00:22:39.039 --> 00:22:44.000
such as YouTube, Tik Tok, Google,

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:46.159
LinkedIn, Amazon KDP, and Instagram use

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:49.120
fair algorithms like this, not just

00:22:46.159 --> 00:22:51.280
Etsy, which is great. However, there is

00:22:49.120 --> 00:22:53.280
one downside, and that is that if the AI

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:55.039
algorithm gets it wrong and chooses the

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:57.200
wrong group of people to test your

00:22:55.039 --> 00:22:59.679
product with, then the test will fizzle

00:22:57.200 --> 00:23:01.840
and it will flop. So something that I

00:22:59.679 --> 00:23:04.400
think is very important to do is to use

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:06.159
AI chat bots like Chat Gvt, Gemini or

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:08.400
Claude to help you optimize your

00:23:06.159 --> 00:23:10.559
products or content to make it easy for

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:13.120
this algorithm to figure out who to show

00:23:10.559 --> 00:23:15.440
it to. So for Etsy, I like to upload a

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.520
photo of what I'm going to list and sell

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:20.080
and ask the AI to create a listing

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:22.880
title, description, and tags optimized

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:26.301
for AI recommendation algorithms. And

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:28.080
look, it can do that for me. Easy. Nice.

